<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/wilson.rs. std only. SU(2) Wilson lattice gauge theory on a torus::Torus, action S = beta sum_p (1 - a0(U_p)), U_p = U(x,mu) U(x+mu,nu) U(x+nu,mu)^dagger U(x,nu)^dagger, links indexed by Torus::link_index. Struct Lattice { torus, links: Vec<Quaternion>, beta, seed, replica, sweep } with cold and hot (Haar, sweep counter -1 stream) starts. staple(link) = sum over nu != mu of U(x+mu,nu) U(x+nu,mu)^dagger U(x,nu)^dagger + U(x+mu-nu,nu)^dagger U(x-nu,mu)^dagger U(x-nu,nu), so the local action is beta a0(U(x,mu) staple). One sweep = for each direction mu, for each parity of the site coordinate sum, update all those links in parallel (they share no plaquette when every side length is even; return an error from new if any side is odd) with std::thread::scope over chunks; each link update uses the stream Stream::new(seed, sweep, link index, replica), so results do not depend on the thread count. heat_bath_sweep, overrelax_sweep, and a combined update (one heat bath then n_or over-relaxation sweeps). Observables: plaquette average; rectangular Wilson loops W(R,T) averaged over all positions and planes (mu,nu) with mu < nu, both orientations; Creutz ratio chi(R,T) = -ln(W(R,T) W(R-1,T-1) / (W(R,T-1) W(R-1,T))). Independent tests: tests/wilson_2d.rs (2D plaquette against character::torus_plaquette at several beta, within 5 jackknife errors; result independent of thread count bit for bit; broken heat bath fails), tests/wilson_4d.rs (gauge invariance of observables under a random gauge transformation to 1e-12; strong-coupling slope beta/4 at beta = 0.1).
